{"term":"ideal","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ce214f0f36e9c35caa","definition":"Pertaining to ideas, or to a given idea.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["conceptual","notional"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:417822fe1f239addac","definition":"Existing only in the mind; conceptual, imaginary.","example":"The idea of ghosts is ridiculous in the extreme; and if you continue to be swayed by ideal terrors —","pos":"adj","synonyms":["conceptual","imaginary"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7a252b5d0a5623a803","definition":"Optimal; being the best possibility.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["best","optimal","optimum"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2706b8217686765174","definition":"Perfect, flawless, having no defects.","example":"1751 April 13, Samuel Johnson, The Rambler, Number 112, reprinted in 1825, The Works of Samuel Johnson, LL. D., Volume 1, Jones & Company, page 194,\nThere will always be a wide interval between practical and ideal excellence; […] .","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:68b38d69f27a3a9c53","definition":"Teaching or relating to the doctrine of idealism.","example":"the ideal theory or philosophy","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:20b4b3758413433740","definition":"Not actually present, but considered as present when limits at infinity are included.","example":"ideal point","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d3591e1121c7d3bbc4","definition":"A perfect standard of beauty, intellect etc., or a standard of excellence to aim at.","example":"Varvara Andreevna, when I was very young, I set before myself the ideal of the woman I loved and should be happy to call my wife.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["order ideal"],"antonyms":["filter"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal","different ideal","factor ideal","fractional ideal","Frink ideal","ideal lattice","lattice ideal","left ideal","minimal ideal","Platonic ideal","primary ideal","prime ideal","principal ideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0e88069663adddb64a","definition":"A two-sided ideal; a subset of a ring which is closed under both left and right multiplication by elements of the ring.","example":"Let #92;mathbb#123;Z#125; be the ring of integers and let 2#92;mathbb#123;Z#125; be its ideal of even integers. Then the quotient ring #92;mathbb#123;Z#125;#47;2#92;mathbb#123;Z#125; is a Boolean ring.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["order ideal"],"antonyms":["filter"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal","different ideal","factor ideal","fractional ideal","Frink ideal","ideal lattice","lattice ideal","left ideal","minimal ideal","Platonic ideal","primary ideal","prime ideal","principal ideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5b618f8a1ede839d12","definition":"A non-empty lower set (of a partially ordered set) which is closed under binary suprema (a.k.a. joins).","example":"An ideal A of L is called complete if it contains all least upper bounds of its subsets that exist in L. Bishop and Schreiner [80] studied conditions under which joins of ideals in the lattices of all ideals and of all complete ideals coincide.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["order ideal"],"antonyms":["filter"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal","different ideal","factor ideal","fractional ideal","Frink ideal","ideal lattice","lattice ideal","left ideal","minimal ideal","Platonic ideal","primary ideal","prime ideal","principal ideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7ce470bd0f38228813","definition":"A collection of sets, considered small or negligible, such that every subset of each member and the union of any two members are also members of the collection.","example":"Formally, an ideal I of a given set X is a nonempty subset of the powerset #92;mathcal#123;P#125;(X) such that: (1)#92;#92;emptyset#92;inI, (2)#92;A#92;inI#92;andB#92;subseteqA#92;impliesB#92;inI and (3)#92;A,B#92;inI#92;impliesA#92;cupB#92;inI.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["order ideal"],"antonyms":["filter"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal","different ideal","factor ideal","fractional ideal","Frink ideal","ideal lattice","lattice ideal","left ideal","minimal ideal","Platonic ideal","primary ideal","prime ideal","principal ideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aa74d7b8886987abf8","definition":"A Lie subalgebra (subspace that is closed under the Lie bracket) 𝖍 of a given Lie algebra 𝖌 such that the Lie bracket [𝖌,𝖍] is a subset of 𝖍.","example":"If 𝖌 is a Lie algebra, 𝖍 is an ideal and the Lie algebras 𝖍 and 𝖌/𝖍 are solvable, then 𝖌 is solvable.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["Lie ideal"],"antonyms":["filter"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal","different ideal","factor ideal","fractional ideal","Frink ideal","ideal lattice","lattice ideal","left ideal","minimal ideal","Platonic ideal","primary ideal","prime ideal","principal ideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:12f5474fffad2eeba6","definition":"A subsemigroup with the property that if any semigroup element outside of it is added to any one of its members, the result must lie outside of it.","example":"The set of natural numbers with multiplication as the monoid operation (instead of addition) has multiplicative ideals, such as, for example, the set {1, 3, 9, 27, 81, ...}. If any member of it is multiplied by a number which is not a power of 3 then the result will not be a power of three.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["order ideal"],"antonyms":["filter"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal","different ideal","factor ideal","fractional ideal","Frink ideal","ideal lattice","lattice ideal","left ideal","minimal ideal","Platonic ideal","primary ideal","prime ideal","principal ideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d74b221b58e43ca7ed","definition":"A city in Georgia, United States.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coideal","counterideal","hyperideal","ideal gas","ideal gas law","ideal mixture","idealness","ideal number","ideal point","ideal polyhedron","ideal-seeking behavior","ideal solution","ideal triangle","ideal-typical","idele","nonideal","non-ideal gas","unideal","different ideal","factor ideal","fractional ideal","Frink ideal","ideal lattice","lattice ideal","left ideal","minimal ideal","Platonic ideal","primary ideal","prime ideal","principal ideal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktion